      "payload": "{\"model_calls\":1,\"phase\":\"preparation\",\"plan\":{\"A\":\"Optimize prefix-frequency counting while initially preserving the baseline traversal. Compare reserved unordered_map with a reusable flat open-addressed table, using generation tags or touched-slot clearing to avoid per-band allocation. Size tables for at most scan_length+1 distinct prefixes; measure capacity and clearing trade-offs. Preserve full-key collision checks and signed keys. Seed frequency[0]=1, query frequency[s-k] before incrementing frequency[s], including when k=0. Compact 32-bit keys/frequencies are safe under the published bounds, but the answer must remain 64-bit. Deliver complete correct variants with isolated measurements.\",\"B\":\"Optimize geometry and memory locality independently of A. Pair boundaries along the smaller dimension, reducing complexity to O(min(M,N)^2*max(M,N)). Orient storage so each inner scan reads contiguous data rather than traversing the baseline's strided ps rows. Compare boundary-major prefix arrays against incrementally accumulated band sums. Preserve general signed-input prefix-frequency counting; negative entries invalidate unconditional sliding-window methods. Measure transpose/preprocessing costs and both square and rectangular behavior without assuming benchmark dimensions.\",\"C\":\"Research CPU parallelism using only threading supported by the unchanged build, with at most four workers. Distribute independent boundary pairs or start-boundary groups; compare balanced static partitioning with coarse dynamic scheduling because triangular outer loops are imbalanced. Give every worker private frequency storage, scratch space and a 64-bit subtotal; reduce only after completion. Avoid inner-loop synchronization and false sharing. Measure one, two and four workers, including launch overhead. Consider a serial fallback based on estimated operation count, not particular test cases.\",\"G\":\"Integrate only correct programs produced by A/B/C, preserving stdin/stdout and all fixed evaluation constraints. Retain the baseline and strongest standalone candidate. Measure compatible combinations within the existing budget rather than assuming additive speedups. Coordinate orientation, hash capacity and worker-local storage; incremental band accumulation favors grouped starts, whereas prefix arrays permit arbitrary pair scheduling. Validate through the unchanged oracle/tests and review correctness for signed values, k=0, degenerate dimensions and maximal counts. Select the best measured complete program; reject slower integrations and unnecessary complexity.\",\"analysis\":\"All roles target the supplied Problem A submatrix counter, not the other contest problems. The only measured program is the correct baseline: four correctness cases and mean runtime 0.2705307 s, with samples spanning approximately 0.265–0.274 s. No optimized gains or hotspot profiles are available. Source inspection suggests three complementary hypotheses: unordered_map allocation/repeated lookups are expensive, fixed column pairing and strided prefix access waste work/locality, and independent bands permit four-core parallelism on ARM64. These are hypotheses requiring measurement. Every valid input must remain correct, including negative entries and targets; counts can reach 249500250000 and require 64-bit accumulation. Keep compiler, tests, oracle, budgets and target unchanged.\"},\"request_sha256\":\"7ab3b4e3ed50c8928503a7fc081236212dff05de6d1bc36cc008a07bb96aa769\",\"response\":{\"data\":{\"A\":\"Optimize prefix-frequency counting while initially preserving the baseline traversal. Compare reserved unordered_map with a reusable flat open-addressed table, using generation tags or touched-slot clearing to avoid per-band allocation. Size tables for at most scan_length+1 distinct prefixes; measure capacity and clearing trade-offs. Preserve full-key collision checks and signed keys. Seed frequency[0]=1, query frequency[s-k] before incrementing frequency[s], including when k=0. Compact 32-bit keys/frequencies are safe under the published bounds, but the answer must remain 64-bit. Deliver complete correct variants with isolated measurements.\",\"B\":\"Optimize geometry and memory locality independently of A. Pair boundaries along the smaller dimension, reducing complexity to O(min(M,N)^2*max(M,N)). Orient storage so each inner scan reads contiguous data rather than traversing the baseline's strided ps rows. Compare boundary-major prefix arrays against incrementally accumulated band sums. Preserve general signed-input prefix-frequency counting; negative entries invalidate unconditional sliding-window methods. Measure transpose/preprocessing costs and both square and rectangular behavior without assuming benchmark dimensions.\",\"C\":\"Research CPU parallelism using only threading supported by the unchanged build, with at most four workers. Distribute independent boundary pairs or start-boundary groups; compare balanced static partitioning with coarse dynamic scheduling because triangular outer loops are imbalanced. Give every worker private frequency storage, scratch space and a 64-bit subtotal; reduce only after completion. Avoid inner-loop synchronization and false sharing. Measure one, two and four workers, including launch overhead. Consider a serial fallback based on estimated operation count, not particular test cases.\",\"G\":\"Integrate only correct programs produced by A/B/C, preserving stdin/stdout and all fixed evaluation constraints. Retain the baseline and strongest standalone candidate. Measure compatible combinations within the existing budget rather than assuming additive speedups. Coordinate orientation, hash capacity and worker-local storage; incremental band accumulation favors grouped starts, whereas prefix arrays permit arbitrary pair scheduling. Validate through the unchanged oracle/tests and review correctness for signed values, k=0, degenerate dimensions and maximal counts. Select the best measured complete program; reject slower integrations and unnecessary complexity.\",\"analysis\":\"All roles target the supplied Problem A submatrix counter, not the other contest problems. The only measured program is the correct baseline: four correctness cases and mean runtime 0.2705307 s, with samples spanning approximately 0.265–0.274 s. No optimized gains or hotspot profiles are available. Source inspection suggests three complementary hypotheses: unordered_map allocation/repeated lookups are expensive, fixed column pairing and strided prefix access waste work/locality, and independent bands permit four-core parallelism on ARM64. These are hypotheses requiring measurement. Every valid input must remain correct, including negative entries and targets; counts can reach 249500250000 and require 64-bit accumulation. Keep compiler, tests, oracle, budgets and target unchanged.\"},\"error\":null,\"infrastructure_error\":false,\"model\":\"gpt-6.1-sol\",\"nonce\":\"46341f3833d44474a52b294b16db72e8\",\"protocol\":\"hpc-forest-codex-mailbox-v1\",\"reasoning_effort\":\"max\",\"request_sha256\":\"7ab3b4e3ed50c8928503a7fc081236212dff05de6d1bc36cc008a07bb96aa769\",\"session_id\":\"a80da638e1054b3a9d13f66e5787f89f\",\"usage\":{\"cached_tokens_included_in_input\":true,\"codex_jsonl_sha256\":\"05e24a667760508d5e94d2f688c9f1c8a56968fa3737c77862bb812f2dd5a4e7\",\"events\":[{\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"cached_input_tokens\":0,\"input_tokens\":10011,\"output_tokens\":3721,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":3106}],\"llm_calls\":1,\"model_requested\":\"gpt-6.1-sol\",\"reasoning_effort_requested\":\"max\",\"token_accounting\":\"exact\",\"tokens\":13732,\"tool_events\":[]}},\"status\":\"complete\"}",
