      "id": 17,
      "kind": "mother_usage",
      "payload": "{\"model_calls\":1,\"phase\":\"synthesis\",\"plan\":{\"A\":\"Own the prefix-frequency kernel, starting from ee5199465a9f4b23. Preserve collision resolution, full-key equality, bounded occupancy and storage reuse. Compare touched-slot clearing against bulk clearing; consider fixed-capacity scratch storage to remove vector bookkeeping. Explore a generic k=0 specialization that adds the previous frequency and increments through one probe, while retaining the general signed-k path. Change one mechanism at a time. Stored keys safely fit int32: absolute prefixes are at most 998001000 and prefix-minus-k at most 1098001000. Keep answers 64-bit and preserve frequency[0]=1 and query-before-increment ordering.\",\"B\":\"Own orientation, preprocessing and scan layout. Evaluate layout changes against the frozen ee5199465a9f4b23 frequency kernel so unordered_map does not mask their effects. Pair the smaller dimension and scan the larger. Prioritize the boundary-major summed-area approach from 25274ce7bdb840a8: compare its separate vectorizable key-generation pass with directly subtracting boundary prefixes inside the frequency loop. Retain incremental contiguous bands as a comparison, not an assumed improvement. Never vectorize across dependent frequency updates. If budget remains, provide an independently measured variant disabling iostream synchronization and cin tying; the source uses only C++ streams.\",\"C\":\"Own worker scheduling around the frozen compact-hash kernel. Start from the successful cyclic assignment in 1e468278ec7b4072, with private tables, private scratch and 64-bit subtotals. Compare serial, two-worker and four-worker execution within existing runtime limits. Reassess the serial crossover because faster hashing changes thread-launch amortization; do not blindly retain 131072 visits. Compare cyclic starts with statically balanced triangular pair ranges, mapping each worker's range once. Deprioritize the measured slower atomic queue. Use only mechanisms supported by the unchanged build, cap workers at four, and finish shared preprocessing before launching workers.\",\"G\":\"Use ee5199465a9f4b23 at 0.08839 s as the incumbent. Integrate transformations deliberately rather than concatenating whole-file diffs. Prioritize compact hashing plus cyclic threading, then compact hashing plus the best layout; attempt the three-way combination only as budget permits. Measure each complete program through the unchanged validation and timing procedure, including input, preprocessing and startup. Recompute table capacity, work estimates and scheduling from the actual scan and paired dimensions after orientation changes. Keep mutable frequency and scratch storage worker-private. Preserve negative-value support, exact output and 64-bit totals—the maximum answer is 249500250000. Retain the fastest validated standalone candidate if integrations regress; change no tests, oracle, compiler, budgets or target.\",\"analysis\":\"Only Problem A matches the supplied source. Baseline time is 0.27053 s. Compact hashing achieved 0.08839 s, about 3.06x faster; cyclic threading achieved 0.10460 s. The best layout-only variant reached 0.24712 s, while atomic-queue scheduling regressed to 0.33698 s. Thus frequency storage is the strongest measured lever, with static parallelism the next promising component. Layout gains may become more visible after hashing improves, but no supplied measurement establishes that interaction. Aggregate timings reveal neither input shapes nor value distributions, so avoid assumptions about them and do not predict additive gains.\"},\"request_sha256\":\"7c6172bcc4fe648f44344d353f05a27f9c120e4773826dbc94280d73510273d7\",\"response\":{\"data\":{\"A\":\"Own the prefix-frequency kernel, starting from ee5199465a9f4b23. Preserve collision resolution, full-key equality, bounded occupancy and storage reuse. Compare touched-slot clearing against bulk clearing; consider fixed-capacity scratch storage to remove vector bookkeeping. Explore a generic k=0 specialization that adds the previous frequency and increments through one probe, while retaining the general signed-k path. Change one mechanism at a time. Stored keys safely fit int32: absolute prefixes are at most 998001000 and prefix-minus-k at most 1098001000. Keep answers 64-bit and preserve frequency[0]=1 and query-before-increment ordering.\",\"B\":\"Own orientation, preprocessing and scan layout. Evaluate layout changes against the frozen ee5199465a9f4b23 frequency kernel so unordered_map does not mask their effects. Pair the smaller dimension and scan the larger. Prioritize the boundary-major summed-area approach from 25274ce7bdb840a8: compare its separate vectorizable key-generation pass with directly subtracting boundary prefixes inside the frequency loop. Retain incremental contiguous bands as a comparison, not an assumed improvement. Never vectorize across dependent frequency updates. If budget remains, provide an independently measured variant disabling iostream synchronization and cin tying; the source uses only C++ streams.\",\"C\":\"Own worker scheduling around the frozen compact-hash kernel. Start from the successful cyclic assignment in 1e468278ec7b4072, with private tables, private scratch and 64-bit subtotals. Compare serial, two-worker and four-worker execution within existing runtime limits. Reassess the serial crossover because faster hashing changes thread-launch amortization; do not blindly retain 131072 visits. Compare cyclic starts with statically balanced triangular pair ranges, mapping each worker's range once. Deprioritize the measured slower atomic queue. Use only mechanisms supported by the unchanged build, cap workers at four, and finish shared preprocessing before launching workers.\",\"G\":\"Use ee5199465a9f4b23 at 0.08839 s as the incumbent. Integrate transformations deliberately rather than concatenating whole-file diffs. Prioritize compact hashing plus cyclic threading, then compact hashing plus the best layout; attempt the three-way combination only as budget permits. Measure each complete program through the unchanged validation and timing procedure, including input, preprocessing and startup. Recompute table capacity, work estimates and scheduling from the actual scan and paired dimensions after orientation changes. Keep mutable frequency and scratch storage worker-private. Preserve negative-value support, exact output and 64-bit totals—the maximum answer is 249500250000. Retain the fastest validated standalone candidate if integrations regress; change no tests, oracle, compiler, budgets or target.\",\"analysis\":\"Only Problem A matches the supplied source. Baseline time is 0.27053 s. Compact hashing achieved 0.08839 s, about 3.06x faster; cyclic threading achieved 0.10460 s. The best layout-only variant reached 0.24712 s, while atomic-queue scheduling regressed to 0.33698 s. Thus frequency storage is the strongest measured lever, with static parallelism the next promising component. Layout gains may become more visible after hashing improves, but no supplied measurement establishes that interaction. Aggregate timings reveal neither input shapes nor value distributions, so avoid assumptions about them and do not predict additive gains.\"},\"error\":null,\"infrastructure_error\":false,\"model\":\"gpt-6.1-sol\",\"nonce\":\"c0c0ca6f8ded4c609c8945e366f3d635\",\"protocol\":\"hpc-forest-codex-mailbox-v1\",\"reasoning_effort\":\"max\",\"request_sha256\":\"7c6172bcc4fe648f44344d353f05a27f9c120e4773826dbc94280d73510273d7\",\"session_id\":\"a80da638e1054b3a9d13f66e5787f89f\",\"usage\":{\"cached_tokens_included_in_input\":true,\"codex_jsonl_sha256\":\"f918af839e55a8599a857ad4d2d03e86290c2c3ab07da05d4af748a9a5d0f45b\",\"events\":[{\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"cached_input_tokens\":0,\"input_tokens\":17328,\"output_tokens\":4788,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":4070}],\"llm_calls\":1,\"model_requested\":\"gpt-6.1-sol\",\"reasoning_effort_requested\":\"max\",\"toke